From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:06:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 099/147] hjviewer: a dialog takes the back press with its own
 cancel, screen readers stay inside it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

UX-M2, the API (critic 4-2: in early, so that other lanes' new dialogs pass it):
- U63: OverlayDialogManager.show takes onBack, which an HJViewer dialog sets to its [취소] or
  [닫기]; without it a backDismiss dialog closes and an upstream dialog swallows the press, as
  before. The interceptor (hjvAddDialogBack, hjv_phone.dart) is added with ifNotYetIntercepted:
  the dialog added last takes the press and the ones below it do not, so one back press closes
  one dialog; while the app lock (W13) holds back presses, which runs first by its zIndex, no
  dialog under the cover takes one.
- U59 (the overlay part): the dialog's overlay entry is wrapped in BlockSemantics and a Semantics
  that scopes a route (hjvDialogScope), so TalkBack, VoiceOver and Narrator do not move to the
  home behind an open dialog. The mask is a plain colour without semantics, so it needs no
  ExcludeSemantics.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
